{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>These are the names of the men.</b> From the tribe of Levi no spy was sent, because it had no portion in the land." "<b>And Moshe called Hoshea son of Nun Yehoshua.</b> Not that he called him Yehoshua now, but rather the meaning is that Moshe had already called him Yehoshua when he became his attendant and found favor in his eyes — for such is the custom, as we find with Avraham and Sarah and Yaakov, Daniel, Chananiah, Mishael, and Azariah, Tzidkiah who was previously called Mataniah, and Nechemiah who was called Hatach. And one may say that he changed his name because he needed to be among the spies and to pass through the land of Amalek by the name Hoshea."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:17:45.687509895Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}